      "statusChangeID": "6373cb87e1b9ee63eb7c0d90",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "not a bug",
      "value": "Hey there, this generally happens when world creators put objects on the \"Player\" or \"PlayerLocal\" layers.\nIf a world puts something on a player layer, a mirror cannot distinguish it from an actual player. This affects world mirrors that are configured with those layers too, not just the Personal Mirror.\nWhile this can lead to weird issues like what's reported here, we can't change anything here without breaking other user content. Only world authors can fix this by moving those objects to other layers and being careful about that going forward.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
